          "id": "s8Zle",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.4.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-10-06\n1. PURPOSE\nStart a design in one of two ways (UI-29): pick a ready-made base and adjust it at once, without an expert; or describe a piece of furniture (photos, words, the rough space) with an optional expert the person connects with their own key. The bases never need the expert.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nOpening the app with no design.\n3. SCREENS (columns are the steps; every screen here is a proposal, except the last one of step 3)\n- Step 1 · Home (in code, UI-79): the library of every base (53). Library: the header (the logo goes Home, the expert's status, Ajustes), the kraft hero with one title and one line, then the search by name across the full width and the rooms as chips with a count, the note \"Ancho × fondo × alto.\" and the cards in four columns (a sketch drawn from the pieces, the name, the size in cm); \"Diseña el tuyo\" floats at the bottom right until the door is in view. End of the list: the bar pinned with its edge, the last cards, the band \"¿No está el tuyo?\" with a filled \"Diseña el tuyo\" (expert or not) and the footer. Room chosen: Entrada, three bases, the door right after.\n- Step 2 · Adjust your base (the bases path; proposal, UI-29): after choosing a base, before the Studio, a short step with the base's 3D and only the questions its ficha allows: where it will go (the space in cm, optional, the base's own measures shown as the starting point), what it holds (counters for what the ficha says can change: drawers, doors, open niches for this sideboard; each base shows its own, for example shelves and doors for the shoe rack, drawers for the bed), and the finish; a live summary of sheets and approximate cost; \"Abrir en el Studio\" and \"Saltar y usar la base tal cual\". NEW strings: \"¿Dónde lo vas a poner?\", \"¿Qué lleva?\", \"¿Cómo lo quieres?\", \"Lo que se puede cambiar lo dice la ficha de este mueble.\", \"Abrir en el Studio\", \"Saltar y usar la base tal cual\". Open: that the questions come from the ficha is a design decision the code does not have yet (today the plan sheet lists every field of the module), and so are the limits of each counter.\n- Step 3 · Connect the expert: the step over the dimmed Home (the library), opened from the header pill or from the form's callout; and its state when a key is already saved (\"Tus llaves están guardadas\": use it or \"Usar una llave nueva\"). The passphrase is optional: with it the key is saved encrypted, without it the key lasts the tab. No \"where to get a key\" path for now.\n- Step 4 · Describe your furniture: without an expert (a callout whose button is a primary \"Conectar experto\" with \"Ver bases\" under it, and \"Conectar experto\" as the form's button; the simulated expert is not offered here, D58), empty (\"Describe tu mueble o agrega una foto\" on the disabled button), ready (\"Diseñar mi mueble\"). Kind, description, the space in cm, photos, a way back to the bases. With photos: the description's label becomes \"¿Algo que el experto deba saber?\" (the code's wording when there are photos) with an optional hint (NEW), the photos are the code's tiles (view, note, read state), and the button stays \"Diseñar mi mueble\".\n- Step 5 · Analyzing: the original sketch and stages, the clock under the sketch, a history of real steps in a footer that fades upward.\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nThe main button of the custom path is disabled until there are 15 characters or a photo (Capture.tsx); the space is asked in cm and the code takes mm today; each photo is read when added.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/capture/{Home,Capture,Analyzing}.tsx, src/ui/settings/{Settings,Keys}.tsx, src/ports/Preferences.ts (PRESETS). Home's strings are all in code (Home.tsx, catalog.ts, shell/AppHeader.tsx, shell/AppFooter.tsx). NEW strings, not in code: \"Conecta tu experto\" with its sub-line and \"Conectar\", the form's sub-line, the space section, the disabled-button labels and the expert-decides wording (\"Que el experto lo decida\").\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nThe mobile band applies as is. Not drawn: Home with an expert connected (the pill reads \"Experto conectado\" with a filled dot and the door loses \"Necesita tu experto conectado; las bases no.\"), no base matching the search (drawn on mobile), a room plus words with no match (\"Ninguna base de ese cuarto tiene «…» en su nombre.\"), a base whose plan does not resolve (a cube icon in place of the sketch), \"Usar el experto simulado\" in the connect dialog (debug access only), reading failed and design failed (they wait in the mobile \"To review\" column), the correcting state of Analyzing and the end that opens the Studio, and the motion (the turn of the sketches, the fade and scroll of the history).\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-29, UI-30, UI-32, UI-35, UI-79\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
